A data structure that maps keys to values, for O(1) (constant-time) _average_ lookup, insert, and delete. Behind the scenes, it uses an array and a hash function to compute an index (bucket) from the key, where the value is stored. Collisions (two keys hashing to the same bucket) are handled via chaining (linked lists) or open addressing (probing for the next free slot).
